/E (The literature on automated AD classification spans three broad architectural families: custom end-to-end CNNs trained from scratch, transfer learning pipelines built on large pretrained networks, and hybrid models that combine deep feature extraction with classical classifiers. Each family presents distinct trade-offs in terms of data requirements, computational cost, interpretability, and generalisation.)
