615 0 obj
<<
/Title (normal \(CN\) classification and 97.5% on a multi-class task. The authors demonstrate that careful tuning of convolutional filter sizes, dropout rates, and batch normalisation can compensate for the reduced parameter count relative to deeper transfer-learning models. However, the absence of any explainability mechanism and its restriction to ADNI data limit direct applicability to the Kaggle four-class scenario targeted by this project. El-Latif et al. [5] further challenged the assumption that architectural depth correlates with performance, proposing a seven-layer lightweight CNN that achieves 99.22% binary accuracy and 95.93% multi-class accuracy on the Kaggle dataset  a directly comparable experimental setting to the present work. The key insight is that simpler architectures, when paired with appropriate data augmentation, can match deeper networks while reducing memory and inference cost, which is a practical advantage for clinical deployment. The limitation is that lightweight designs may underfit on more heterogeneous real-world data where richer feature hierarchies are needed. Ahmed et al. [3] introduced DAD-Net, a five-block custom CNN that directly addresses class imbalance through ADASYN synthetic oversampling, raising accuracy from 90.0% to 99.22% on the Kaggle dataset. This result is significant because it isolates the contribution of the class-balancing strategy: on identical architecture, ADASYN alone accounts for nearly a ten-point accuracy gain. By contrast, the current project's chosen Kaggle variant is already class-equalised through augmentation, reducing but not eliminating this concern. DAD-Net's strength lies in its demonstrated sensitivity to data distribution; its weakness is the absence of any XAI component, which the present project aims to remedy. Comparing these three custom designs, AbdulAzeem et al. [2] provides the strongest binary result but lacks multi-class generalisation and explainability; El-Latif et al. [5] offers the most practically deployable design for four-class Kaggle classification; and Ahmed et al. [3] contributes the clearest evidence that data balancing strategy is at least as important as architecture choice  a lesson directly applicable to this project's preprocessing pipeline. 2.2 Transfer Learning and Pretrained Architectures)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 445 0 R
/Next 647 0 R
>>
